A||N||11||Cozmo||How do you open the decklid with no key?||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||11-08-2001||06:03 PM||||Got An '88 Coupe today with no decklid key. The engine grilles are gone, if I unbolt the hinges can I get in thru there enough to get it open?<BR>If that isn't possible, any ideas or suggestions on how to get it open?<P> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnF||11-08-2001||06:08 PM||||Power decklid?  Remove rocker from inst. panel and apply 12vdc (Batt Charger or something) to the lower two contacts.  POP!  Door opens!<P>Manual decklid? Cuss a lot! When that doesn't work (and it probably won't) drill out the key hole or punch it out with a hammer and tap of some kind.  Keys and locks are available commercially to replace the damage.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||b52buf||11-08-2001||06:26 PM||||The deck lid key should be the same as your door key,assuming you have the door key. In the long run it probably be wiser and cheaper to call a locksmith and have him do his magic.Before you cause additional damage.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||11-08-2001||07:07 PM||||Careful with those hinges. If the torsion bar lets go (i.e., you undo the wrong bolts) it WILL take the shortest path THROUGH your back window  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Best bet is to jimmy the lock... That always works for me, if I have a spare hour  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But yeah, I'd call the locksmith... $30 and you're in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000004||JohnF||11-08-2001||07:25 PM||||On an '88, the door key is the same as the engine lid.  The ignition is stand alone!<P>Any GM dealer can cut you a complete set of keys for any Fiero for which you can prove ownership (title, insurance papers, whatever the dealership wants).  Take the VIN and your proof of ownership and let the parts man do his magic.  <P>Good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000005||cadaver||11-10-2001||09:38 PM||||Hey John. Why pull the switch panel to apply 12v just plug it into the cig lighter and hit the switch.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shinerdc||11-10-2001||11:42 PM||||have an 84...manual key/decklid...same problem...sprayed with oil undercoater....the foamy stuff flows all around what it contacts...2 days later...offered the 12 year 5 bucks to get it open and presto...lucked out....think the oil spray loosed up any dry lubricants...suggest spray and patience before a drill bit...||||reg||1
Z||000007||The Prezzzz||11-11-2001||11:19 AM||||Easy to open! look were the battery sits you said grills are off so you shouldn't have a problem, right next to the dick lid hindge is the plug in connector for hood unplug and use 12v to pop the lid||||reg||1
Z||000008||Sootah||11-11-2001||11:58 AM||||While were on the subject of frooked locks, the passenger side door lock on my 85 GT is busted. You can stick the key in and just keep turnin. You can lock/unlock from the inside but the key apperatus is broked.<P>Me want help. Actually, I know I can't do that myself, so how much is it going to cost me to have GM or a locksmith slap a new dealie in there?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||5
Z||000009||JohnF||11-11-2001||12:17 PM||||The original questioner hasn't responded but, seems as if he NO power anything.  So, applying 12VDC to anything won't help.<P>Like I said, prove ownership and provide the VIN to any GM parts counter employee and they will make a complete set of keys for about $5.00 and 5 minutes.  Can't be easier!<P>It's all on their computer.||||reg||10
Z||000010||Monkeyman||11-11-2001||01:01 PM||||JohnF--Assuming the original locks haven't been changed.<P>Sootah--You can do it yourself.  If I can, anyone can.  It's unlikely a locksmith will even know how to change the lock cylinder (which is probably what needs to be done) and a dealership will probably charge $100 (might as well do both sides so your locks match unless a handfull of keys impresses you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).  You can buy the lock cyls for less than $15 at Autozone (same locks the dealers use, I'm sure) and you can do the job in an hour or two.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cozmo||11-11-2001||02:13 PM||||The car doesn't have power trunk release.<BR>I ended up drilling the lock out, no damage to the decklid.<BR>I have a set of full power doors and a decklid WITH matching keys I'm going to install.<BR>This is an '88 Coupe that will soon be a Cadero... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks for all the ideas,<BR>BobC ||||reg||1
